    "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
    "heading": "MOVING AND FIGHTING UNDERWATER",
    "lineStart": 4875,
    "lineEnd": 4881,
    "pdfPageStart": 92,
    "pdfPageEnd": 92
  },
  "rulesText": "By default, attack rolls made while the attacker is underwater have disadvantage.\n\nFor creatures that can’t breathe underwater, use a standard countdown (3) to track how long they can hold their breath. Advance the countdown whenever the PC takes an action. In addition if they fail a roll or roll with Fear while underwater, you can spend your GM move to advance it an additional time—or twice, if they rolled a failure with Fear.\n\nOnce the countdown ends, the underwater PC must mark a Stress whenever they take an action.",
  "htmlPage": {
